IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- must I register for GST, what is a
-- taxable supply, how much GST is on it, and what input tax credit I get: s 9-5 (taxable supplies), s 9-20 (enterprise),
-- s 9-40 (who pays), ss 9-70 and 9-75 (10% of the value), ss 11-5, 11-15, 11-20, 11-25 and 11-30 (creditable acquisitions
-- and input tax credits), ss 7-5 and 17-5 (the net amount), s 23-5 (who is required to be registered), s 23-10 (who may be
-- registered), s 23-15 (the registration turnover threshold), s 25-1 (apply within 21 days), s 27-5 (3 month tax periods),
-- ss 29-70(2) and 29-80 (tax invoices), s 31-5, 31-8 and 31-10 (GST returns and when they are due), s 33-3 (when payment
-- is due), s 144-5 (taxi travel: registration regardless of turnover), ss 188-10, 188-15, 188-20, 188-25 and 188-30 (GST
-- turnover, current and projected), and the s 195-1 definition of "taxi travel".
--
-- SEAT: the sole trader or business owner -- the entity that carries on the enterprise, asking "Must I register for GST?".
-- The Act puts the duty on that entity ("It is the entity that carries on the enterprise that is required to be
-- registered", s 23-5 note), so for a business run through a company the "I" of each question is the company, asked by
-- its owner. Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 96, compilation date 1 January 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 72, 2025 (Register id
-- C2026C00081), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.txt, with the formulas in ss 9-75(1), 11-30(3)
-- and 17-5(1) from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.formulas.md (transcribed by hand on 21 October 2026 from the
-- Word rendering of volume 1 of the same compilation).
--
-- THE THRESHOLD IS SET BY REGULATIONS THAT ARE NOT DEPOSITED. Section 23-15 says "$50,000; or such higher amount as the
-- regulations specify" ($100,000 or higher for a non-profit body). The A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax)
-- Regulations 2019 are not in the deposit, so the higher amount they specify is an INPUT. The worked cases use $75,000
-- and $150,000, the figures the life scenarios assume; they are not read from any deposited text.
--
-- THE TEXT DEPOSIT DROPS EVERY FORMULA set as an image: s 9-75(1) (the value of a taxable supply), s 11-30(3) (a partly
-- creditable acquisition) and s 17-5(1) (the net amount) each say "as follows:" or "using the following formula:" and
-- then "where:". The formulas are transcribed in C2004A00446.formulas.md: "Price x 10/11"; "Full input tax credit x Extent
-- of creditable purpose x Extent of consideration"; "GST - Input tax credits". They are what the first baseline had
-- reconstructed from the surrounding words, now confirmed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Chapter 3 beyond asking, as a fact, how much of a supply is GST-free or input taxed (Divisions 38, 40);
-- Chapter 4's special rules (GST groups, branches, non-residents, margin scheme, gambling, second-hand goods, the
-- Division 151 annual tax periods, the Division 162 instalments); Division 15 (importations); Divisions 19 and 21
-- (adjustments); Subdivision 29-B (cash accounting) and attribution beyond s 29-10(3); s 25-10 (date of effect) and
-- Subdivision 25-B (cancellation); s 27-10 and 27-15 (monthly tax periods are an input); s 188-22 to 188-24, 188-32 to
-- 188-40; the machinery (Part 1, Chapter 5 and 6). Borrowed terms are asked as facts: "business" in its ordinary sense,
-- "taxi" and "limousine" (undefined), "non-profit body", whether a supply is GST-free or input taxed, whether the
-- supply to me is a taxable supply of the seller, and whether a supply is connected with the indirect tax zone.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
-- Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 -- registration, taxable supplies and input tax credits`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER @desc A number
      `b` IS A NUMBER @desc Another number
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 9-20 -- enterprise`

-- s 9-20(1): "An enterprise is an activity, or series of activities, done: (a) in the form of a business; or (b) in the
-- form of an adventure or concern in the nature of trade; or (c) on a regular or continuous basis, in the form of a lease,
-- licence or other grant of an interest in property; ..." (Gloss: roughly, running a business or a trading venture, or
-- regularly letting property. Paragraphs (d) to (h) -- gift funds, super funds, charities, governments -- are not this
-- seat and are not offered.) s 195-1: "business includes any profession, trade, employment, vocation or calling, but does
-- not include occupation as an employee."
DECLARE `Form of activity` IS ONE OF
    `a business`
    `an adventure or concern in the nature of trade`
    `a regular lease, licence or grant of an interest in property`
    `none of these`

-- s 9-20(2): "However, enterprise does not include an activity, or series of activities, done: (a) by a person as an
-- employee ...; or (b) as a private recreational pursuit or hobby; or (c) by an individual ..., or a partnership (all or
-- most of the members of which are individuals), without a reasonable expectation of profit or gain; ..."
DECLARE `My activity` HAS
    `form of activity`                                          IS A `Form of activity`
    `done as an employee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a private recreational pursuit or hobby`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an individual, or a partnership mostly of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable expectation of profit or gain`                  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `form` IS A `Form of activity` @desc The form the activity takes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a form s 9-20(1) lists` IF
    CONSIDER `form`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Am I carrying on an enterprise (s 9-20)?
GIVEN `my activity` IS A `My activity` @desc What you do, how, and in what capacity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I carrying on an enterprise` IF
        `is a form s 9-20(1) lists` (`my activity`'s `form of activity`)
    AND (NOT `my activity`'s `done as an employee`)
    AND (NOT `my activity`'s `a private recreational pursuit or hobby`)
    AND (NOT (    `my activity`'s `I am an individual, or a partnership mostly of individuals`
              AND (NOT `my activity`'s `reasonable expectation of profit or gain`)))

§§ `s 23-15 -- the registration turnover threshold`

-- s 23-15: "(1) Your registration turnover threshold (unless you are a non-profit body) is: (a) $50,000; or (b) such higher
-- amount as the regulations specify. (2) Your registration turnover threshold if you are a non-profit body is: (a)
-- $100,000; or (b) such higher amount as the regulations specify." The regulations are not deposited: the higher amount
-- is an input (0 if none is specified).
@export What is my GST registration turnover threshold, in dollars (s 23-15)?
GIVEN `I am a non-profit body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a non-profit body
      `the higher amount the regulations specify` IS A NUMBER @desc The higher threshold the GST Regulations specify for an entity like you, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my registration turnover threshold` IS
    IF `I am a non-profit body`
    THEN `the greater of` 100000 `the higher amount the regulations specify`
    ELSE `the greater of` 50000  `the higher amount the regulations specify`

§§ `ss 9-70, 9-75, 188-30 -- value and the 10% rate`

-- s 9-70: "The amount of GST on a taxable supply is 10% of the value of the taxable supply." s 9-75(1): the value is given
-- by the formula "Price x 10/11" (transcribed; the text deposit drops it); price is "the sum of (a) so far as the consideration ... is ... money -- the amount
-- (without any discount for the amount of GST (if any) payable on the supply) ...". From the section's example (a
-- $22,000 car: "$22,000 x 10/11 = $20,000", GST $2,000). (Gloss: the price includes the GST, so the
-- GST is one eleventh of the price.)
@export What is the value of my taxable supply, in dollars (s 9-75)?
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the supply, in dollars, including any GST
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the value of a taxable supply` IS (`price` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 11

-- s 188-30: "For the purposes only of this Division, the value of a supply that is not a taxable supply is taken to be
-- 11/10 of what would be the value of the supply if it were a taxable supply." (Gloss: for the turnover test, a supply
-- that bears no GST counts at its full price.)
@export What does one of my supplies count for in my GST turnover, in dollars (ss 9-75, 188-30)?
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the supply, in dollars, including any GST
      `it is a taxable supply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supply is a taxable supply
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What does a supply count for in my turnover` IS
    IF `it is a taxable supply`
    THEN `What is the value of a taxable supply` `price`
    ELSE (`price` TIMES 10 TIMES 11) DIVIDED BY (11 TIMES 10)
    -- 11/10 of the 10/11 value, multiplied out before dividing so that the result is exact: the full price.

§§ `Division 188 -- GST turnover`

-- One set of supplies, over one 12-month window, as the person states it. Only supplies made for consideration and in
-- connection with the enterprise are counted (s 188-15(1)(b), (c); s 188-20(1)(b), (c)); the person states only those.
DECLARE `Supplies in a 12-month window` HAS
    `price of all my supplies made or likely to be made` IS A NUMBER
    `of which, input taxed or not connected with the indirect tax zone` IS A NUMBER
    `of which, GST-free` IS A NUMBER
    `of which, capital assets sold or supplies because I am closing or shrinking` IS A NUMBER

-- INFERENCE: whether a supply is "taxable" turns on whether I am "registered, or required to be registered" (s 9-5(d)),
-- which turns on my turnover. The circle is broken here by treating the supplies of a person who is NOT registered as
-- not taxable for the turnover test (they bear no GST, s 188-30), and those of a registered person as taxable except the
-- GST-free part.
GIVEN `window` IS A `Supplies in a 12-month window` @desc The supplies in the window
      `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered for GST
      `projected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the projected window (s 188-25 applies only to that)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the turnover of a window` IS
    `What does a supply count for in my turnover` `taxable part` `I am registered`
      PLUS `What does a supply count for in my turnover` (`window`'s `of which, GST-free`) FALSE
    WHERE
        -- Arithmetic is fully parenthesised for readability. (A first draft gave a wrong turnover figure; the orchestrator later checked that the stable l4 treats chained MINUS as left-associative, so the cause lay elsewhere.)
        `excluded` MEANS
            `window`'s `of which, input taxed or not connected with the indirect tax zone`
              PLUS (IF `projected`
                    THEN `window`'s `of which, capital assets sold or supplies because I am closing or shrinking`
                    ELSE 0)
        `taxable part` MEANS
            `the greater of` 0 (`window`'s `price of all my supplies made or likely to be made`
                                 MINUS (`excluded` PLUS `window`'s `of which, GST-free`))

-- s 188-15(1): "Your current GST turnover at a time during a particular month is the sum of the values of all the
-- supplies that you have made, or are likely to make, during the 12 months ending at the end of that month, other than:
-- (a) supplies that are input taxed; or (b) supplies that are not for consideration ...; or (c) supplies that are not made
-- in connection with an enterprise that you carry on." s 188-15(3)(a): disregard "any supply that is not connected with
-- the indirect tax zone".
@export What is my current GST turnover, in dollars (s 188-15)?
GIVEN `last 12 months` IS A `Supplies in a 12-month window` @desc Your supplies in the 12 months ending at the end of this month
      `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered for GST
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my current GST turnover` IS `the turnover of a window` `last 12 months` `I am registered` FALSE

-- s 188-20(1): "Your projected GST turnover at a time during a particular month is the sum of the values of all the
-- supplies that you have made, or are likely to make, during that month and the next 11 months, other than ...". s
-- 188-25: "disregard: (a) any supply ... by way of transfer of ownership of a capital asset of yours; and (b) any supply
-- made ... solely as a consequence of: (i) ceasing to carry on an enterprise; or (ii) substantially and permanently
-- reducing the size or scale of an enterprise."
@export What is my projected GST turnover, in dollars (ss 188-20, 188-25)?
GIVEN `this month and the next 11` IS A `Supplies in a 12-month window` @desc Your supplies this month and the next 11 months
      `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered for GST
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my projected GST turnover` IS `the turnover of a window` `this month and the next 11` `I am registered` TRUE

-- s 188-10(1): "You have a GST turnover that meets a particular turnover threshold if: (a) your current GST turnover is at
-- or above the turnover threshold, and the Commissioner is not satisfied that your projected GST turnover is below the
-- turnover threshold; or (b) your projected GST turnover is at or above the turnover threshold." The Commissioner's
-- satisfaction is asked as a fact.
@export Does my GST turnover meet the threshold (s 188-10(1))?
GIVEN `current GST turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current GST turnover, in dollars
      `projected GST turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc Your projected GST turnover, in dollars
      `the Commissioner is satisfied my projected turnover is below the threshold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that your projected GST turnover is below the threshold
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The turnover threshold, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my GST turnover meet the threshold` IF
       (    `current GST turnover` AT LEAST `threshold`
        AND (NOT `the Commissioner is satisfied my projected turnover is below the threshold`))
    OR `projected GST turnover` AT LEAST `threshold`

§§ `s 144-5 and s 195-1 -- taxi travel`

-- s 195-1: "taxi travel means travel that involves transporting passengers, by taxi or limousine, for fares." "Taxi" and
-- "limousine" are not defined in the Act and are asked as facts. (Gloss: carrying goods or food is not "transporting
-- passengers"; an e-bike is neither a taxi nor a limousine.)
@export Do I supply taxi travel (s 195-1)?
GIVEN `I transport passengers for fares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in your enterprise, you carry passengers for fares
      `by taxi or limousine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry them by taxi or limousine
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I supply taxi travel` IF `I transport passengers for fares` AND `by taxi or limousine`

§§ `ss 23-5, 23-10, 144-5 -- must I register`

-- The facts one entity states, at one time during one month.
DECLARE `My GST facts` HAS
    `my activity`                                  IS A `My activity`
    `I intend to carry on an enterprise from a particular date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a non-profit body`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am registered`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the higher amount the regulations specify`    IS A NUMBER
    `last 12 months`                               IS A `Supplies in a 12-month window`
    `this month and the next 11`                   IS A `Supplies in a 12-month window`
    `the Commissioner is satisfied my projected turnover is below the threshold` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I transport passengers for fares`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `by taxi or limousine`                         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `me` IS A `My GST facts` @desc The facts about you and your enterprise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my GST turnover meets the registration turnover threshold` IF
    `Does my GST turnover meet the threshold`
        (`What is my current GST turnover` (`me`'s `last 12 months`) (`me`'s `I am registered`))
        (`What is my projected GST turnover` (`me`'s `this month and the next 11`) (`me`'s `I am registered`))
        (`me`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied my projected turnover is below the threshold`)
        (`What is my registration turnover threshold` (`me`'s `I am a non-profit body`) (`me`'s `the higher amount the regulations specify`))

DECLARE `Registration answer` IS ONE OF
    `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold`
    `Required to be registered: I supply taxi travel`
    `Not required, but I may register`
    `Not required, and I may register from the date I intend to start`
    `Not required, and not entitled to register: I carry on no enterprise`

-- s 23-5: "You are required to be registered under this Act if: (a) you are carrying on an enterprise; and (b) your GST
-- turnover meets the registration turnover threshold." s 144-5: "(1) You are required to be registered if, in carrying
-- on your enterprise, you supply taxi travel. (2) It does not matter whether: (a) your GST turnover meets the
-- registration turnover threshold ... (3) This section has effect despite section 23-5". s 23-10: "(1) You may be
-- registered ... if you are carrying on an enterprise (whether or not your GST turnover is at, above or below the
-- registration turnover threshold). (2) You may be registered ... if you intend to carry on an enterprise from a
-- particular date."
@export Must I register for GST, and if not, may I (ss 23-5, 23-10, 144-5)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My GST facts` @desc The facts about you and your enterprise
GIVETH A `Registration answer`
DECIDE `Must I register for GST` IS
    IF `Am I carrying on an enterprise` (`me`'s `my activity`)
    THEN IF `Do I supply taxi travel` (`me`'s `I transport passengers for fares`) (`me`'s `by taxi or limousine`)
         THEN `Required to be registered: I supply taxi travel`
         ELSE IF `my GST turnover meets the registration turnover threshold` `me`
              THEN `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold`
              ELSE `Not required, but I may register`
    ELSE IF `me`'s `I intend to carry on an enterprise from a particular date`
         THEN `Not required, and I may register from the date I intend to start`
         ELSE `Not required, and not entitled to register: I carry on no enterprise`

@export Am I required to be registered for GST (ss 23-5, 144-5)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My GST facts` @desc The facts about you and your enterprise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I required to be registered` IF
    CONSIDER `Must I register for GST` `me`
    WHEN `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Required to be registered: I supply taxi travel` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 25-1 -- applying within 21 days`

-- s 25-1: "You must apply, in the approved form, to be registered under this Act if: (a) you are not registered under
-- this Act; and (b) you are required to be registered. You must make your application within 21 days after becoming
-- required to be registered."
@export By when must I apply to register for GST (s 25-1)?
GIVEN `the day I became required to be registered` IS A DATE @desc The day you became required to be registered, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to register` IS `the day I became required to be registered` PLUS 21

GIVEN `me` IS A `My GST facts` @desc The facts about you and your enterprise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to register now` IF
    `Am I required to be registered` `me` AND (NOT `me`'s `I am registered`)

-- The same duty, as a regulative rule: the entity must apply within 21 days of becoming required.
DECLARE `GST party` IS ONE OF `the entity required to be registered`
DECLARE `GST act` IS ONE OF `apply in the approved form to be registered`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `GST party` `GST act`
DECIDE `the s 25-1 duty to apply` IS
    PARTY `the entity required to be registered`
    MUST  `apply in the approved form to be registered`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the entity required to be registered`

§§ `s 9-5 -- taxable supplies; s 9-40 -- who pays`

-- One supply I make.
DECLARE `My supply` HAS
    `price`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `made for consideration`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the course or furtherance of my enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `connected with the indirect tax zone`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `GST-free or input taxed part of the price`   IS A NUMBER

-- s 9-5: "You make a taxable supply if: (a) you make the supply for consideration; and (b) the supply is made in the
-- course or furtherance of an enterprise that you carry on; and (c) the supply is connected with the indirect tax zone;
-- and (d) you are registered, or required to be registered. However, the supply is not a taxable supply to the extent
-- that it is GST-free or input taxed."
@export Is my supply a taxable supply, at least in part (s 9-5)?
GIVEN `the supply` IS A `My supply` @desc The supply you make
      `I am registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my supply a taxable supply` IF
        `the supply`'s `made for consideration`
    AND `the supply`'s `made in the course or furtherance of my enterprise`
    AND `the supply`'s `connected with the indirect tax zone`
    AND `I am registered or required to be registered`
    AND `the supply`'s `GST-free or input taxed part of the price` LESS THAN `the supply`'s `price`

-- s 9-40: "You must pay the GST payable on any taxable supply that you make." With ss 9-70 and 9-75: 10% of the value,
-- on the taxable part of the price only.
@export How much GST must I pay on my supply, in dollars (ss 9-40, 9-70, 9-75)?
GIVEN `the supply` IS A `My supply` @desc The supply you make
      `I am registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much GST must I pay on my supply` IS
    IF `Is my supply a taxable supply` `the supply` `I am registered or required to be registered`
    THEN (`What is the value of a taxable supply`
              (`the supply`'s `price` MINUS `the supply`'s `GST-free or input taxed part of the price`)
            TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

§§ `Division 11 -- creditable acquisitions and input tax credits`

-- One thing I acquire.
DECLARE `My acquisition` HAS
    `price`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the supply to me is a taxable supply`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I provide or am liable to provide consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percent acquired in carrying on my enterprise`   IS A NUMBER
    `percent of the consideration I provide`          IS A NUMBER

-- s 11-15: "(1) You acquire a thing for a creditable purpose to the extent that you acquire it in carrying on your
-- enterprise. (2) However, you do not acquire the thing for a creditable purpose to the extent that: (a) the acquisition
-- relates to making supplies that would be input taxed; or (b) the acquisition is of a private or domestic nature." The
-- person states the percentage after (2).
-- s 11-5: "You make a creditable acquisition if: (a) you acquire anything solely or partly for a creditable purpose; and
-- (b) the supply of the thing to you is a taxable supply; and (c) you provide, or are liable to provide, consideration
-- for the supply; and (d) you are registered, or required to be registered."
@export Is my purchase a creditable acquisition (s 11-5)?
GIVEN `the acquisition` IS A `My acquisition` @desc The thing you acquired
      `I am registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my purchase a creditable acquisition` IF
        `the acquisition`'s `percent acquired in carrying on my enterprise` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the acquisition`'s `the supply to me is a taxable supply`
    AND `the acquisition`'s `I provide or am liable to provide consideration`
    AND `I am registered or required to be registered`

-- s 11-20: "You are entitled to the input tax credit for any creditable acquisition that you make." s 11-25: "an amount
-- equal to the GST payable on the supply of the thing acquired. However, the amount of the input tax credit is reduced if
-- the acquisition is only partly creditable." s 11-30(3): "Full input tax credit x Extent of creditable purpose x Extent of
-- consideration" (transcribed; the text deposit drops it), the two extents being percentages. The GST payable on the supply to me is taken to be on
-- the whole price (the seller's GST-free part, if any, is not asked).
@export How much input tax credit do I get for my purchase, in dollars (ss 11-20, 11-25, 11-30)?
GIVEN `the acquisition` IS A `My acquisition` @desc The thing you acquired
      `I am registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much input tax credit do I get` IS
    IF `Is my purchase a creditable acquisition` `the acquisition` `I am registered or required to be registered`
    THEN (((`full input tax credit` TIMES `the acquisition`'s `percent acquired in carrying on my enterprise`) DIVIDED BY 100)
            TIMES `the acquisition`'s `percent of the consideration I provide`) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `full input tax credit` MEANS
            (`What is the value of a taxable supply` (`the acquisition`'s `price`) TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 29-10(3): without a tax invoice when I lodge, the credit "is not attributable to that tax period" but to the first
-- period for which I lodge holding it. s 29-80(1): that rule does not apply where the value of the supply "does not exceed
-- $50, or such higher amount as the regulations specify" (input; 0 if none).
@export Can I claim this input tax credit in this period's return (ss 29-10(3), 29-80)?
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price of what you acquired, in dollars, including GST
      `I hold a tax invoice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a tax invoice for it when you lodge the return
      `the higher amount the regulations specify` IS A NUMBER @desc The higher low-value limit the GST Regulations specify, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim the credit in this return` IF
       `I hold a tax invoice`
    OR `What is the value of a taxable supply` `price` AT MOST `the greater of` 50 `the higher amount the regulations specify`

-- s 29-70(2): "The supplier of a taxable supply must, within 28 days after the recipient of the supply requests it, give
-- to the recipient a tax invoice for the supply".
@export By when must I give my customer a tax invoice (s 29-70(2))?
GIVEN `the day my customer asked for it` IS A DATE @desc The day the recipient of your taxable supply asked for a tax invoice, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give a tax invoice` IS `the day my customer asked for it` PLUS 28

§§ `ss 7-5, 17-5 -- the net amount`

-- s 7-5: "Amounts of GST and amounts of input tax credits are set off against each other to produce a net amount for a
-- tax period". s 17-5(1): "GST - Input tax credits" (transcribed; the text deposit drops it), the GST and the input tax
-- credits attributable to the period, before adjustments (s 17-5(2), not encoded). s 7-15: a positive net
-- amount I pay; a negative one is refunded to me.
@export What is my net amount for the tax period, in dollars (a negative amount is a refund) (ss 7-5, 17-5)?
GIVEN `GST on my taxable supplies in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The GST on your taxable supplies attributable to the period, in dollars
      `input tax credits in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc Your input tax credits attributable to the period, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my net amount` IS `GST on my taxable supplies in the period` MINUS `input tax credits in the period`

§§ `ss 27-5, 31-5, 31-8, 31-10, 33-3 -- tax periods, returns and payment`

-- s 31-5: "(1) If you are registered or required to be registered, you must give to the Commissioner a GST return for each
-- tax period. (2) You must give the return whether or not: (a) your net amount for the tax period is zero; ..."
@export Must I lodge a GST return for each tax period (s 31-5)?
GIVEN `I am registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a GST return` IF `I am registered or required to be registered`

-- s 27-5: "The tax periods that apply to you are each period of 3 months ending on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September or 31
-- December in any year, except to the extent that: (a) an election is in force under section 27-10; or (b) the
-- Commissioner determines otherwise". Whether monthly periods apply is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Quarter` IS ONE OF
    `the quarter ending 31 March`
    `the quarter ending 30 June`
    `the quarter ending 30 September`
    `the quarter ending 31 December`

-- s 31-8(1) table (and s 33-3, the same days for payment): "1 September -- the following 28 October; 1 December -- the
-- following 28 February; 1 March -- the following 28 April; 1 June -- the following 28 July", keyed on a day that "falls
-- within the quarterly tax period". (Gloss: the return and payment are due on the 28th of the second month after the
-- quarter, except the December quarter, due 28 February.)
@export By when must I lodge my quarterly GST return and pay (ss 31-8, 33-3)?
GIVEN `the quarter` IS A `Quarter` @desc The quarterly tax period
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the quarter ends
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I lodge my quarterly return` IS
    CONSIDER `the quarter`
    WHEN `the quarter ending 31 March`     THEN Date 28 4  `the year`
    WHEN `the quarter ending 30 June`      THEN Date 28 7  `the year`
    WHEN `the quarter ending 30 September` THEN Date 28 10 `the year`
    WHEN `the quarter ending 31 December`  THEN Date 28 2  (`the year` PLUS 1)

-- s 31-10(1): for a tax period other than a quarterly one, "on or before the 21st day of the month following the end of
-- that tax period".
@export By when must I lodge my monthly GST return (s 31-10)?
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month the tax period ends, 1 to 12
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year the tax period ends
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I lodge my monthly return` IS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 12
    THEN Date 21 1 (`the year` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date 21 (`the month` PLUS 1) `the year`
